3.Tell Me About a Time You Had a Conflict at Work


During a project to migrate from Java 8 to Java 17, I faced a conflict about using new features like `var` and `record`.

First Attempt (Failure 1):
I started using `var` for local variables to make the code shorter. However, some team members found it confusing because they couldn’t see
the types easily. This made code reviews slower.

Second Attempt (Failure 2):
To fix this, I stopped using `var` and used explicit types everywhere. While this made the code clear, it resulted in a lot of repetitive 
code that wasn’t necessary.

Final Solution (Success):
I then decided to find a middle ground. I used `var` only in simple cases where the type was obvious. I also used `record` for data objects
to reduce boilerplate code. This helped keep the code modern and easy to read.

In the end, this balanced approach improved our code while keeping it clear and maintainable."

